  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 16th August 2006 the erection of a rear roof extension incorporating hip to gable end and one roof light in the front elevation was lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nThe development falls within the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class B of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 because the volume of the proposed extensions are below the maximum 50 cubic metre allowance for additions to the roof, and bellow the 70 cubic metre total allowance for this type of house.\r\n"
